# {{variable}} interpolation, resolved from the "key = value" declarations
# below -- these are global: declared once in the prelude (before the first
# "###"), inherited by every request in this file, in the URL, headers, or
# body. A request can also declare its own local variable of the same name
# to override the global value just for that one request.
#
# Run `make httpbin-up` first. See 1_basic.http for plain requests and
# 3_scripting.http for pre-request/post-request scripting.

host = http://localhost:8080
greeting = hello

###
# @name Get
GET {{host}}/get?greeting={{greeting}} HTTP/1.1
Accept: application/json

###
# @name Post
POST {{host}}/post HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{auth_token}}

{
  "name": "John",
  "greeting": "{{greeting}}"
}
